<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Efficiency on KevCaz's Website</title><link>https://kevcaz.github.io/tags/efficiency/</link><description>Recent content in Efficiency on KevCaz's Website</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-us</language><copyright>Content under CC0 1.0 Universal unless otherwise specified.</copyright><lastBuildDate>Sun, 18 Nov 2018 00:00:00 +0000</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://kevcaz.github.io/tags/efficiency/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>A bug in the command wrapper of r-core-base 3.5.1-1+b2</title><link>https://kevcaz.github.io/notes/2018/11/2018-11-18_a_bug_in/</link><pubDate>Sun, 18 Nov 2018 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://kevcaz.github.io/notes/2018/11/2018-11-18_a_bug_in/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Today, as I working on a post, I got this issue when using the R command wrapper:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;div style="color:#575279;background-color:#faf4ed;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;
&lt;table style="border-spacing:0;padding:0;margin:0;border:0;"&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="vertical-align:top;padding:0;margin:0;border:0;"&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#575279;background-color:#faf4ed;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span style="white-space:pre;-webkit-user-select:none;user-select:none;margin-right:0.4em;padding:0 0.4em 0 0.4em;color:#7f7f7f"&gt;1
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="white-space:pre;-webkit-user-select:none;user-select:none;margin-right:0.4em;padding:0 0.4em 0 0.4em;color:#7f7f7f"&gt;2
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="white-space:pre;-webkit-user-select:none;user-select:none;margin-right:0.4em;padding:0 0.4em 0 0.4em;color:#7f7f7f"&gt;3
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td style="vertical-align:top;padding:0;margin:0;border:0;;width:100%"&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#575279;background-color:#faf4ed;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-R" data-lang="R"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#797593"&gt;$&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#d7827e"&gt;Rscript&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#797593"&gt;--&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#d7827e"&gt;no&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#797593"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#d7827e"&gt;site&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#797593"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#d7827e"&gt;file&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#797593"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#d7827e"&gt;e&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#ea9d34"&gt;&amp;#39;blogdown::serve_site()&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#797593"&gt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#d7827e"&gt;usr&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#797593"&gt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#d7827e"&gt;lib&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#797593"&gt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#d7827e"&gt;R&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#797593"&gt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#d7827e"&gt;bin&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#797593"&gt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#d7827e"&gt;R&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#797593"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#d7827e"&gt;line&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#ea9d34"&gt;193&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#797593"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#797593"&gt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#d7827e"&gt;usr&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#797593"&gt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#d7827e"&gt;bin&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#797593"&gt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#d7827e"&gt;sed&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#797593"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#d7827e"&gt;No&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#d7827e"&gt;such&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#d7827e"&gt;file&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#d7827e"&gt;or&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#d7827e"&gt;directory&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#d7827e"&gt;ERROR&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#797593"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#d7827e"&gt;option&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#ea9d34"&gt;&amp;#39;-e&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#d7827e"&gt;requires&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#d7827e"&gt;a&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#d7827e"&gt;non&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#797593"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#d7827e"&gt;empty&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#d7827e"&gt;argument&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;I did not understand what happened so I decided to google it! The &lt;a href="https://www.mail-archive.com/search?l=debian-bugs-dist@lists.debian.org&amp;amp;q=subject:%22Bug%23913982%5C%3A&amp;#43;r%5C-base%5C-core%5C%3A&amp;#43;R&amp;#43;executable&amp;#43;wrapper&amp;#43;scripts&amp;#43;hard%5C-code&amp;#43;the&amp;#43;wrong&amp;#43;path&amp;#43;to&amp;#43;sed.%22&amp;amp;o=newest&amp;amp;f=1"&gt;bug was already identified and reported &amp;#x1f604;&lt;/a&gt;. A side note to mention that several packages now imports
&lt;a href="https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/callr/index.html"&gt;callr&lt;/a&gt; (for instance
&lt;a href="https://pkgdown.r-lib.org/"&gt;pkgdown&lt;/a&gt;) and as it uses the R command wrapper
(if I understand correctly) the current bug actually affects several different
packages. A simple example is when I try to rebuild the website of &lt;a href="https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/rcites/index.html"&gt;rcites&lt;/a&gt;
(using pkgdown):&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Make your conditional statements efficient!</title><link>https://kevcaz.github.io/notes/2018/10/2018-10-30_make_your_conditional/</link><pubDate>Tue, 30 Oct 2018 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://kevcaz.github.io/notes/2018/10/2018-10-30_make_your_conditional/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Recently, I was looking at an R function and found a if statement that looks something like this:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;div style="color:#575279;background-color:#faf4ed;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;
&lt;table style="border-spacing:0;padding:0;margin:0;border:0;"&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="vertical-align:top;padding:0;margin:0;border:0;"&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#575279;background-color:#faf4ed;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span style="white-space:pre;-webkit-user-select:none;user-select:none;margin-right:0.4em;padding:0 0.4em 0 0.4em;color:#7f7f7f"&gt;1
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="white-space:pre;-webkit-user-select:none;user-select:none;margin-right:0.4em;padding:0 0.4em 0 0.4em;color:#7f7f7f"&gt;2
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="white-space:pre;-webkit-user-select:none;user-select:none;margin-right:0.4em;padding:0 0.4em 0 0.4em;color:#7f7f7f"&gt;3
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td style="vertical-align:top;padding:0;margin:0;border:0;;width:100%"&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#575279;background-color:#faf4ed;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-R" data-lang="R"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#286983"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#797593"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#d7827e"&gt;length&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#797593"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#d7827e"&gt;which&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#797593"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#d7827e"&gt;names&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#797593"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#d7827e"&gt;df&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#797593"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#797593"&gt;==&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#ea9d34"&gt;&amp;#34;entry&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#797593"&gt;))&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#797593"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#ea9d34"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#797593"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#797593"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#9893a5"&gt;# [...]&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#797593"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;I guess this is common way of doing it as it matches well with a way of looking
at the problem: &amp;ldquo;if I want to test the presence of a column &amp;ldquo;entry&amp;rdquo; in a data frame
(&lt;code&gt;df&lt;/code&gt;), I can check if there is more at least one name that match &amp;ldquo;entry&amp;rdquo;.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>